    "region": "Germany",
    "description": "The city of Fulda is one of the principal cities of the federal state of Hesse in central Germany. Situated on the Fulda River between the Rhön and Vogelsberg mountains, Fulda is known for its sumptuous baroque architecture, historic churches and religious relics. Founded by followers of the Anglo-Saxon Saint Boniface (c. AD 675–754), best known for his missionary work to the Germanic parts of the Frankish Empire in the eighth century, Fulda remains an important German bishopric. While best known as a place of Christian pilgrimage in the Medieval period, Fulda's thriving modern economy based on small to medium-sized manufacturing companies has yielded one of the lowest unemployment rates of any region within a European Union member state.",
