    "name": "Grand Canyon-Parashant National Monument",
    "region": "U.S.A.",
    "description": "Grand Canyon-Parashant National Monument, established in 2000, consists of 42,000 hectares of land on the “Arizona Strip,” the portion of Arizona lying north of the Colorado River. The monument is bounded to the south by the Grand Canyon and on the west by the Arizona-Nevada border. At the junction of the Colorado Plateau, Mojave Desert and Great Basin, it is among the most isolated of the federally managed land units in the contiguous 48 states. Parashant is a land of no paved roads, limited structures, four Wilderness areas and pristine night skies.",
