    "name": "Great Basin National Park",
    "region": "U.S.A.",
    "description": "Great Basin National Park is comprised of 31,230 hectares (77,180 acres) of U.S. federal lands centered on the eponymous Great Basin, a dry and mountainous region between the Sierra Nevada of California and the Wasatch Mountains of Utah, USA. Situated approximately 470 kilometers (290 miles) north of Las Vegas, Nevada, the Park protects stands of ancient bristlecone pine trees, the world’s oldest known non-clonal organisms, and the Lehman Caves at the base of 3,982-meter (13,063-foot) Wheeler Peak. The Highland Ridge Wilderness, lying just south of the Park, brings the total area of contiguous protected lands to 590.0 km 2 (227.8 mi 2 ).",
