    "name": "Greater Big Bend International Dark Sky Reserve",
    "region": "Mexico, U.S.A.",
    "description": "At over 9 million acres, the Greater Big Bend International Dark Sky Reserve is currently the world’s largest Reserve and protected Dark Sky Place. The Reserve spans from Fort Davis, Texas, to the Rio Grande River at the US/Mexico international border, and includes three protected areas in Mexico – Maderas del Carmen, Ocampo, and Cañón de Santa Elena – making it the world’s first bi-national International Dark Sky Reserve. The protected landscape encompasses a vast area of the Chihuahuan Desert characterized by diverse desert habitat and wildlife, complex geology, and a rich human history. Significant cultural and natural resources dot the landscape of the Reserve representing thousands of years of human occupation and lifeways specially adapted to the rugged desert environment.",
