    "name": "Kaikōura",
    "region": "New Zealand",
    "description": "The Kaikōura Dark Sky Sanctuary is situated in a remote region of the South Island, Aotearoa New Zealand. Offering some of the country's most breathtaking natural landscapes, Kaikōura’s majestic mountains lie within two ranges rising straight from the Pacific Ocean. The sanctuary covers 98% of the local district (approximately 2,039 km²), with over half of the area under protection from the Department of Conservation. Filled with stars, celestial wonders, and a stunningly clear Milky Way, it celebrates pristine dark skies that have a sky quality measuring an average of 21.58 magnitude per square arcsecond.",
