    "region": "U.S.A.",
    "description": "Weber County North Fork Park is situated on 1,000 hectares of mountain valley land in Utah’s Wasatch Range north of the Ogden area. The park attracts cross-country skiers in the winter months with 12 km of groomed skiing trails at elevations between 1,770 and 1,890 meters elevation. It is also a winter venue for Nordic skiing events. In the summer, the park welcomes thousands of guests at six large group areas and 181 individual campsites, and offers hike/bike trails, sand volleyball courts, horseshoe pits, horse corrals, and more.",
    "category": "Park",
    "officialUrl": "https://darksky.org/places/north-fork-park-dark-sky-park/"
