    "description": "Palm Beach Headland is located on the outer edge of the Sydney region and the northernmost tip of Palm Beach, Australia. The designated area comprises Governor Phillip Park and Barrenjoey Headland. Named by Governor Phillip, it offers beach activities, picnics, hikes to Barrenjoey Lighthouse, and access to Pittwater for small boats. Known as Summer Bay from the TV show &#8220;Home and Away,&#8221; it hosts events by the North Palm Beach Surf Life Saving Club, including carnivals and training. The Urban Night Sky Place (UNSP) covers 62 hectares and incorporates Governor Phillip Park and Barrenjoey Headland which is part of Ku-ring-gai Chase National Park.",
