    "description": "Shenzhen Fairy Lake Botanical Garden , Chinese Academy of Sciences, is located on the eastern outskirts of Shenzhen's Luohu District, between Wutong Mountain and Shenzhen Reservoir. Its interwoven mountains, hills, and waterways create exceptional natural conditions. Covering about 668 hectares, the garden was founded in 1983 and opened to the public on May 1, 1988. It is a multifunctional botanical garden that integrates ex situ plant conservation and displays, botanical research, science education, and recreation. In recent years, it has welcomed more than four million visitors annually. The garden conserves more than 13,000 plant taxa across 24 specialist gardens and conservation bases. It is home to 131 bird species, including 13 under Class II national protection, as well as squirrels, wild boar, ferret-badgers, snakes, leopard cats, and other wildlife.",
